cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the findings of this paper, please cite it as below."
title: "Amortized Initialization versus Langevin Refinement for Motion-Guided Segmentation: A Controlled Study of Conditional Energy-based Models (EBMs)"
abstract: >-
  A controlled study of conditional energy-based models (EBMs) for motion
  segmentation. We replace long-run Langevin sampling from noise with a
  data-grounded amortized initializer followed by K short Langevin refinement
  steps, and quantify what the learned energy contributes over the initializer
  alone across DAVIS-16, FBMS-59 and SegTrack-v2.
